  "body": "> Let element be the first title element in the SVG namespace that is a child of the root element, if any. If there isn't one, create a title element in the SVG namespace, append it to the root element, and let element be that element. [SVG]\n> https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#document.title\n\nBut the SVG spec says:\n\n> In conforming SVG document fragments, any ‘title’ element should be the first child element of its parent. Note that those implementations that do use ‘title’ to display a tooltip often will only do so if the ‘title’ is indeed the first child element of its parent.\n> http://www.w3.org/TR/SVG/struct.html#DescriptionAndTitleElements\n\nSo I'd think it should be inserted as the first element, not appended.\n\n(I'm currently [implementing this for Gecko](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1213818), which until now didn't support setting document.title for SVG.)\n",
